 ],
 "title": "Functional Programming in Lean",
 "byline": "David Thrane Christiansen \u00b7 Lean FRO, current online edition (updated through 2025; code tested with recent Lean 4 releases), CC BY 4.0",
 "web": true,
 "note": "There is no official PDF of this book; it is published as a website. This breakdown follows the current online edition, so every section links to its page there instead of a PDF page range. Per-chapter \u201cSummary\u201d pages are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words.",
 "summary": "An introduction to Lean 4 as a general-purpose functional programming language, for programmers who want to write real programs rather than proofs. It covers expressions, types, structures, inductive datatypes, polymorphism and strings; compiling and running programs with IO and Lake; type classes, coercions and instance search; monads and do-notation; functors, applicative functors and universes; monad transformers and imperative-style do features; programming with dependent types and indexed families; a short course on induction proofs with tactics (including grind); and finally writing fast code that is also proved correct: tail recursion, termination, bounded indices, in-place array mutation and runtime representations."
}